{"name":"Heather Sachet","hex":"#7b7173","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"heather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen plant, Calluna vulgaris, with spiky leaves and small purple, pink, or white flowers.","A plant in the family Ericaceae."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple colour with a tint of pink and blue."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/heather"},{"term":"sachet","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small scented cloth bag filled with fragrant material such as herbs or potpourri.","A cheesecloth bag of herbs or spices added during cooking and then removed before serving."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sachet"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sachet","blocks":[{"text":"Although its most usual definition is that listed under \"packet\", a sachet can also mean a small scented cloth bag filled with herbs, potpourri, or aromatic ingredients; or a small porous bag or packet containing a material intended to interact with its atmosphere; for example, desiccants are usually packed in sachets which are then placed in larger packages. Cotton, linen or organza are used to create the bag."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Tan_Plaid_Lavender_Sachets.jpg/330px-Tan_Plaid_Lavender_Sachets.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sachet","wikidata":"Q2597618"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Sachets_d%C3%A9shydratants_sodepac.JPG/330px-Sachets_d%C3%A9shydratants_sodepac.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Sachets_d%C3%A9shydratants_sodepac.JPG/330px-Sachets_d%C3%A9shydratants_sodepac.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sachets containing desiccants","link":"https://en.wikipedia.or